    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Bidirectional edge node iterator.</para><para>Iterates over the edge nodes in a list, returning the <ref refid="structEdge" kindref="compound">Edge</ref> when dereferenced. <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1Edge" kindref="compound">Edge</ref> iterators are stable across insert and erase operations. The difference between <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1EdgeIterator" kindref="compound">EdgeIterator</ref> and <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1ConstEdgeIterator" kindref="compound">ConstEdgeIterator</ref> is that the latter returns const references when dereferenced. An <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1EdgeIterator" kindref="compound">EdgeIterator</ref> can be impliciatly converted to a <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1ConstEdgeIterator" kindref="compound">ConstEdgeIterator</ref>, <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1EdgeValueIterator" kindref="compound">EdgeValueIterator</ref>, or <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1ConstEdgeValueIterator" kindref="compound">ConstEdgeValueIterator</ref>. </para>    </detaileddescription>
